# The nextpnr the gateware is placed and routed with (scripts/nextpnr.sh):
# the project's fork, built from source into .tools/nextpnr, used by
# rtl/Makefile in preference to the OSS CAD Suite's.
# Copyright © 2026 Thor H. Linløkken <thj@thj.no>
# License: CERN-OHL-S v2
#
# The fork carries Gowin fixes the suite's nextpnr lacks: timing arcs for
# the DSP cells and the dual-port block RAM's port B address, (with
# upstream since 2026-10-16) arcs for LUT1..LUT3 cells, a third of the
# LUTs of this design, which the pinned suite never timed, and the DSP
# macro exclusion that stops a MULT18X18 sharing a MULTALU36X18's macro
# (the "two arcs with same sink wire" router failures, #162, #183), and
# the DSP control-line fixes of #450: a control net leaves the macro's and
# block's lists when its last cell does (offered upstream, YosysHQ/nextpnr
# #1904), plus a project guard of one RESET net per block and one CLK and
# one CE net per macro, because the pack suite's apicula writes only line
# 0 (YosysHQ/apicula #603); the guard goes with the pin bump to a pack
# suite carrying that fix (docs/gowin_oss_notes.md section 7).
# Measured on main (d03e915), one netlist, the boot self-test per clock
# step: the suite reports 119 MHz and the chip fails from 86; this
# nextpnr reports 72-82 across seeds and the chip holds to 110
# (docs/gowin_oss_notes.md). The fixes are offered upstream
# (YosysHQ/nextpnr #1890, #1891, #1892).
# The chip database is generated with the pack suite's Apicula, so the
# placement and the bitstream generator agree on the chip.
# The place-and-route result (rtl/Makefile: PLACER_BETA, SEED) belongs to
# this commit: change it by editing commit= (the full SHA, which is what
# git can fetch by) and running `make tools`.
repository=HermesOracle/nextpnr
